[
    {
        "content": "<p>There were some very basic algebraic geometry instances that I could not find, and I was wondering if they existed in a different form somewhere in Mathlib. For example, this one:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra_ofAffineHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRingCat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I am not saying that constructing this is very hard. In this case, we have : </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra_ofAffineHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRingCat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">smul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">preimage</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">algebraMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">preimage</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">commutes'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mul_comm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">preimage</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">smul_def'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I was just wondering whether these facts, which are fundamental in AG, appear in some other form in Mathlib. There were a few others as well, like the one below.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finite_of_isFiniteOverField</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↧</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsFinite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 623561853,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1789135245
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For the first kind of instance, you usually do not introduce it yourself, and instead, use <code>Spec.homEquiv</code> (built on top of <code>Spec.preimage</code>) to get first a morphism in <code>CommRingCat</code>, then use the <code>algebraize</code> tactic on the attached ring hom. This is usually done inline within proofs rather than defined externally. You can grep for <code>algebraize</code> inside the <code>AlgebraicGeometry</code> directory to see how it is used in practice.</p>",
        "id": 623567285,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1789136565
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For the second lemma, I think there may be a fairly direct route through the quasi-finite/fiber API.</p>\n<p>For <code>[IsFinite f]</code>, we get <code>LocallyQuasiFinite f</code>, and finite morphisms are affine hence quasi-compact. There is</p>\n<p><code>Scheme.Hom.finite_preimage_singleton</code></p>\n<p>with essentially</p>\n<p><code>(f ⁻¹' {y}).Finite</code></p>\n<p>for a locally quasi-finite, quasi-compact <code>f</code>.</p>\n<p>Also <code>Spec K</code> has a <code>Unique</code> instance when <code>K</code> is a field. So if</p>\n<p><code>f : X ⟶ Spec ↧K</code></p>\n<p>then the preimage of the unique point of <code>Spec K</code> is all of <code>X</code>.</p>\n<p>So I think <code>Finite_of_isFiniteOverField</code> should reduce to something morally like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_finite_univ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">finite_preimage_singleton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↧</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- f ⁻¹' {default} = Set.univ since Spec K is subsingleton</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↧</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Subsingleton</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(modulo whatever simplification is nicest for identifying the unique fiber with <code>Set.univ</code>).</p>\n<p>So it looks like the underlying mathematical fact may already be available through <code>Morphisms.QuasiFinite</code>, even if there isn't a dedicated theorem with exactly the statement you wrote.</p>",
        "id": 623689393,
        "sender_full_name": "Zeping Cheng",
        "timestamp": 1789180576
    },
